oes  tend to transmute things into images of  his own face  something which at least would take some  level of attention to detail which many  alchemists might not have an interesting  thing to note with armstrong  specifically is that he's one of very  few state alchemists who play a major  role which doesn't actually have a main  goal for himself rather he just seems to  want to do good and to help those he  cares about  tim marco is the crystal alchemist and  his original goal as a member of the  military was to create a philosopher's  stone in general he is one of the nicer  characters in the series however he  definitely struggles greatly with ptsd  from the ish fallen war  marco can't really do anything in combat  but his knowledge of philosopher's  stones also extends to destroying them  something which was hugely influential  in the fight with envy sulph jake kimley  the crimson lotus alchemist is all about  explosions this is one of the characters  who was most affected by the split from  2003 to brotherhood while in both  versions he is depicted as being  sadistic  in 2003 he is definitely much more  psychotic while in 2009 he's a bit more  philosophical  still nuts in either version though he  sees explosions as art forms making him  very similar to daedra in naruto except  again  very much more crazy he has his circles  tattooed on his palms and can  effectively clap them together to  trigger an explosion he works very  similar to mustang in all honesty as he  causes alchemic imbalances within things  to cause them to explode he can also  spread this to things that are touching  that object as well so just as mustang  can increase the oxygen and create a  path for the flame to follow kimberley  kinda does this with explosions in the  2003 version is explained that he shifts  the atomic elements within objects  turning them into what is essentially  gun powder  giolio is the silver alchemist he's a  short old dude who is absolutely battle  obsessed and sa